    {
      "id": 181500,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-08-24T02:25:05.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Flow of Fiery Lava just makes the lava hexes on the Volcano hazard spaces.</p><p>Any target entering a lava hex will face a hazard attack, they will face another attack if they end their turn on a lava hex.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>In Scenario 3 Dawn gains the ability (Geothermal Power) to make new Lava hexes, which will then also make hazard attacks against anyone entering that hex or ending their turn on a lava hex.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As Foote said there are problems with Scenario 2.</p><p>The current best rules changes for making it work are:</p><p>1. &nbsp;Only use 5 shards.<br><span>2. &nbsp;Winner of Scenario 1 gets 1 shard in their victory pile. &nbsp;(if you didn't play Scenario 1 have all five carried by citizens)<br>3. &nbsp;The other 4 shards are given to Citizens of the Citizen players choice. &nbsp;(all 4 shards are being carried at the start of the game)<br>4. &nbsp;First team to get 3 shards in their victory pile win.<br>5. &nbsp;The Tachyon rule: &nbsp;When carrying a shard none of a target's actions are unlimited. &nbsp;(Without this Tachyon can win the match single handed, imagine the flash in a game of capture the flag, super speed is kind of broken in that setting)</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:06:16.267Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
